From c5a8d3485bf6b6d804d142123addf2a96e41ffc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:14:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] chat: K2-Horizon takes the generic tool_choice none path

With K2 rendered without tools under none, its think block no longer ends at a
call, and the drops_calls_under_none opt-out skipped the opener cut, so
"Thinking then call directly <ifm|tool_calls>..." leaked the raw call markup
into reasoning_content (found in review of the previous commit).

Remove the opt-out (flag, session branch, chat.h field; K2 was its only user)
so K2 gets the normal none handling: opener cut and ban of single-special-token
openers. K2 also writes Kimi-form calls, which are not grammar triggers (a
trigger would constrain that form under auto), so common_chat_params gets
extra_call_openers, cut under none only.

Test (tests/test-chat.cpp, failing first on both K2 templates):
test_k2_tool_choice_none_cuts_calls covers a call while thinking, after a
closed think block, a Kimi-form call after a closed block and while thinking,
and a plain reply.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
